# Emil Design Engineering

For UI polish, animation decisions, and interaction details, read and follow:

`.cursor/skills/emil-design-eng/SKILL.md`

## When to invoke

- Adding or changing motion (entrance, hover, transitions)
- Reviewing component feel and micro-interactions
- Choosing between CSS vs GSAP for an interaction
- Typography, spacing, or color refinement beyond Figma spec

## Key principles (summary)

- Unseen details compound — polish what users feel, not just see
- CSS for interruptible UI (hovers, toggles); GSAP for orchestrated entrance
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- No `transition: all` — specify exact properties
- Ease-out for elements entering; ease-in for elements exiting
